  - co-rotational formulation
  - fibre beam
  - progressive collapse
abstract: >-
  A structural analysis program for bridges based on the vector form
  intrinsic finite element method. Beams, fibre beams, bars, cables,
  connectors, shells and solids with reinforcement and tendons; dynamic
  relaxation and Newton statics, construction stages, creep, shrinkage and
  relaxation, moving loads and vehicles, seismic excitation, modal and
  buckling analysis, member fracture with separation and contact. Every
  reference case carries a verification contract against closed-form
  solutions, laboratory tests or field measurements.
